<p>How does this help us? We know we need to rearrange the characters on th=
e right of the string, but we don=E2=80=99t know how many to rearrange. Fro=
m now on, let=E2=80=99s refer to the rightmost characters that should be re=
arranged as the <strong>suffix</strong>.</p>
<p>Take the string "abcedda" as an example. We traverse it from right to le=
ft with the <strong>goal of finding the shortest suffix that can be rearran=
ged to form a larger permutation.</strong> The last 4 characters form a non=
-increasing suffix, and cannot be rearranged to make the string larger:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
