<p>And just like that, we found the next lexicographical sequence! The two-=
pointer strategy used in this problem is staged traversal, where we first i=
dentify the pivot, and then identify the rightmost successor relative to it=
.</p>
<p>Many steps are involved in identifying the next lexicographical sequence=
. So, here=E2=80=99s a summary:</p>
<ol>
<li>Locate the pivot.</li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>The pivot is the first character that breaks the non-increasing sequenc=
e from the right of the string.</li>
<li>If no pivot is found, the string is already at its last lexicographical=
